{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JgVrqB6yCF3V16u9qdthvF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Task 02 — Bug fixing: TTL/LRU cache\n2\t\n3\t`ttl_cache.py` is a deliberately faulty implementation. Fix it without changing\n4\tthe public API and add regression tests.\n5\t\n6\tRequired behavior:\n7\t\n8\t- `get(key)` returns the stored value, including falsy values such as `0`, `False`\n9\t  and `None`; it raises `KeyError` only for missing or expired entries.\n10\t- TTL uses the injected monotonic `clock` and expires at `age >= ttl_seconds`.\n11\t- A successful `get` refreshes LRU recency but does not refresh TTL.\n12\t- `put` updates an existing key's value, timestamp and recency.\n13\t- Before enforcing capacity, expired entries are removed.\n14\t- Capacity eviction removes the least recently used live entry.\n15\t- `max_size < 1` and `ttl_seconds <= 0` raise `ValueError`.\n16\t\n17\tRun the tests. Write `RESPONSE.md` with the root causes, fixes, regression cases,\n18\tand exact test result. Work only in this directory.\n19\t\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa1eeb9b-98bf-4405-94aa-7b4e0e19f415","uuid":"a9fb9df3-36c5-49d2-ac00-48a68e1a0366","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:31:23.068Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-arda-projects-agent-evaluation/8413ce30-b544-4ae4-afd6-5f8333042ec1/scratchpad/agent-eval-haiku-5.5/02-bug-fixing/TASK.md","content":"# Task 02 — Bug fixing: TTL/LRU cache\n\n`ttl_cache.py` is a deliberately faulty implementation. Fix it without changing\nthe public API and add regression tests.\n\nRequired behavior:\n\n- `get(key)` returns the stored value, including falsy values such as `0`, `False`\n  and `None`; it raises `KeyError` only for missing or expired entries.\n- TTL uses the injected monotonic `clock` and expires at `age >= ttl_seconds`.\n- A successful `get` refreshes LRU recency but does not refresh TTL.\n- `put` updates an existing key's value, timestamp and recency.\n- Before enforcing capacity, expired entries are removed.\n- Capacity eviction removes the least recently used live entry.\n- `max_size < 1` and `ttl_seconds <= 0` raise `ValueError`.\n\nRun the tests. Write `RESPONSE.md` with the root causes, fixes, regression cases,\nand exact test result. Work only in this directory.\n\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JgVrqB6yCF3V16u9qdthvF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
